  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I personally feel as if one of the main problems with VRChat is that the only servers that are pushed to the top on the world select are the popular ones, or ones that are event related. Personally, I feel as if this makes it extremely hard for new players to find worlds they are actually interested in, introducing them to worlds with people that could be hard to socialize with. For example, if someone really loves playing minigames with other people, why not try to recommend them worlds where they can find fun games as such rather than only showing them the pug and sleeping rooms on the front page. This could be implemented by allowing map creators, when they upload/update their map, to add tags to their worlds. dIf there were recommended worlds based on worlds a person has joined multiple times, then it may help newcomers find communities and worlds that they might have an easier time making friends. This would help spread out the amount of people across all world, allowing smaller worlds to increase in popularity.",
